# WPT conformance runner: the pinned suite checkout and the generated results are
# both reproducible from `tools/wpt/run.ps1`, and the suite is far too large to commit.
tools/wpt/.cache/
tools/wpt/results/

# The WPT runner is its own workspace with its own lock. It is committed rather than
# ignored, because the rule is "any workspace built with `--locked` in CI must have
# its lock tracked" - see the note further down.
# (its lock is currently small; the suite itself lives in tools/wpt/.cache/)
artifacts/
crates/render-core/.artifacts/
bindings/python/python/render_runtime/*.pdb

# Lockfiles for the standalone workspace roots are COMMITTED, not ignored.
# `tests/real_site_tasks` and `tests/wpt_runner` are their own workspace roots, so
# each has its own `Cargo.lock`, and CI builds the harness with `--locked`. An
# ignored lockfile plus `--locked` means cargo refuses to resolve on a clean
# checkout, so the gate fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the code.
# The rule is: any workspace built with `--locked` in CI must have its lock tracked.

